{
  "full_translation_en": "Federal Parliament\nHouse of Representatives, 2082\nSecond Session\nMeeting No. - 44\nFederal\nNepal\nParliament\nNotice - 2\n(Brief details of the meeting proceedings)\nTuesday, Bhadra 2, 2083\nThe meeting of the House of Representatives today commenced at 11:10 AM under the chairmanship of the Right Honourable Speaker Dol Prasad Aryal.\nAt the beginning of the meeting, during the impromptu session, the following Honourable Members expressed their views on contemporary issues including the need for immediate operation of the Jajarkot-Dolpa road under the Bheri Corridor, which is the lifeline of the Dolpa residents, as it has been completely obstructed due to the flood on Shrawan 20; the need to identify the causes of road accidents and take necessary steps to reduce them; the need for timely repair of the electricity and communication services disrupted in the remote areas of Sankhuwasabha and Udaypur due to damage to the transmission lines and towers caused by continuous rainfall in the Bhotkhola Rural Municipality of Sankhuwasabha; the need for the concerned bodies to take timely initiatives to control elephant menace as the destructive activities of wild elephants that entered Nepal from India with a large herd have caused significant damage to the crops and physical structures of farmers in Jhapa; and the need for the government to remove the VAT imposed on electricity consumption and focus on increasing electricity consumption, as electricity is an alternative to traditional energy sources like gas, firewood, and dung cakes:-\nHon. Purna Prasad Limbu\nHon. Dhan Bahadur Buda\nHon. Shriram Neupane\nHon. Prem Bahadur Bayak\nHon. Prakash Pathak\nSubsequently, during the Zero Hour, the following Honourable Members expressed their views on contemporary issues:-\nHon. Balawati Sharma\nHon. Rata Kumari Thapa\nHon. Ranju Neupane\nHon. Basu Maya Tamang\nHon. Rabin Mahato\nHon. Basana Thapa\nHon. Bina Gurung\nHon. Ramesh Kumar Mall\nHon. Buddha Ratna Maharjan\nHon. Ramesh Kumar Sapkota\nHon. Buddhi Prasad Pant\nHon. Ramesh Prasai\nHon. Bharat Kumar Swar\nHon. Rabindra Patel\nHon. Bharat Prasad Parajuli\nHon. Raj Kishor Mahato\nHon. Bharat Bahadur Khadka\nHon. Rajan Gautam\nHon. Bhim Kumari Buda Magar\nHon. Rajiv Khatri\nHon. Madan Krishna Shrestha\nHon. Rajesh Kumar Chaudhary\nHon. Manmaya B.K.\nHon. Radhika Ramtel\nHon. Manish Khanal\nHon. Ram Lama\nHon. Ringala Yadav\nHon. Madhav Bahadur Thapa\nHon. Rina Upreti\nHon. Mohan Lal Acharya\nHon. Rukesh Ranjit\nHon. Yagya Bahadur Bogati\nHon. Rukmini Devi Koirala\nHon. Rachana Khatiwada Khatri\nHon. Rekha Kumari Yadav\nHon. Rajani Shrestha\nHon. Renuka Kaucha\nThereafter, during the Special Time, the following Honourable Members expressed their views on contemporary issues:-\nHon. Krantishikha Dhital\nHon. Jagat Prasad Joshi\nHon. Prakash Singh Karki\nHon. Lalita Kumari\nHon. Rima Bishwakarma\nHon. Rajendra Kumar Rai\nHon. Uttam Prasad Poudel\nHon. Barsaman Pun\nHon. Ganesh Dhimal\nHon. Harka Raj Rai\nHon. Gyan Bahadur Shahi\nHon. Bishwaraj Pokharel\nHon. Bodhnarayan Shrestha\nHon. Deepak Kumar Sah (Mahottari)\nHon. Narendra Kumar Kerung\nHon. Govinda Panthi\nHon. Bhumika Limbu Subba\nHon. Aaren Rai\nHon. Samina Miyan\nHon. Thakur Singh Tharu\nHon. Karishma Kathariya\nHon. Vishnu Bahadur Khadka\nHon. Eliza Gurung\nMeanwhile, after Hon. Tika Sangraula finished speaking, Hon. Sajida Khatun Siddiki raised a point of order, stating that the opposition would never support the government's wrongdoings and that the prevailing lawlessness in the country was happening under the government's protection, and demanded that the government respond regarding the police firing in Siraha. Immediately thereafter, Hon. Tika Sangraula, raising a point of order and drawing attention to Rule 21(b) of the Regulations, requested that the word \"your police\" used by Hon. Sajida Khatun Siddiki during her speech be expunged from the parliamentary record. Similarly, Hon. Ringala Yadav objected to the use of the words \"goons and anarchists\" for the previous government and stated that the current government is perpetuating lawlessness in the country.\nThereafter, the Right Honourable Speaker informed the House about a minor amendment made to the agenda for today's proceedings.\nSubsequently, under the Question and Answer program as per Chapter-8 of the House of Representatives Regulations, 2083, in the Q&A program related to the Ministry of Energy, Water Resources and Irrigation, Hon. Minister of Energy, Water Resources and Irrigation, Biraj Bhakta Shrestha, responded to the question asked by Hon. Basana Thapa (Question No. 6).\nMeanwhile, when Hon. Harka Raj Rai questioned why a written question was asked when it was meant to be oral, the Right Honourable Speaker drew attention to the provision in Chapter-8 of the House of Representatives Regulations, 2083, that questions asked orally by Honourable Members would be answered orally.\nAfter that, the Honourable Minister of Culture, Tourism and Civil Aviation, Khadak Raj Poudel, answered the questions asked by Hon. Nishkal Rai (Questions No. 7 and 8) and also provided supplementary answers.\nSubsequently, the Honourable Minister of Agriculture, Forest and Environment, Gita Chaudhary, answered the questions asked by Hon. Nishkal Rai (Questions No. 9 and 10) and also provided supplementary answers.\nThereafter, the Honourable Minister of Foreign Affairs, Shishir Khanal, answered the questions asked by Hon. Nishkal Rai (Questions No. 4 and 5).\nSubsequently, the Honourable Minister of Foreign Affairs, Shishir Khanal, responding to questions raised during the impromptu, zero, and special hours, informed the House about issues including the construction of own buildings for Nepali missions abroad, management of local staff, rescue of Nepalis in distress, advancement of the process for constructing embassy buildings in Canberra, Australia, Riyadh, Saudi Arabia, and Bangkok, Thailand, the rescue of only 860 Nepalis from Cambodia, and the provision of a fund of 15 crore rupees for the rescue of those who went abroad illegally and are in trouble, and for bringing their bodies back to Nepal.\nThereafter, Hon. Asika Tamang sought time to ask a question, expressing dissatisfaction with the minister's response, but the Right Honourable Speaker informed that ministers would not be present to answer questions raised during impromptu, zero, and special hours.\nSubsequently, on behalf of the Right Honourable Prime Minister, Pushpa Kamal Dahal 'Prachanda', the Honourable Minister of Law, Justice and Parliamentary Affairs, Sobita Gautam, presented the \"Seventh Annual Report of the Tharu Commission (Shrawan 2081 - Ashadh 2082)\" to the House.\nThereafter, the Honourable Minister of Foreign Affairs, Shishir Khanal, presented the proposal \"Consider the Passport (First Amendment) Bill, 2083\".\nThereafter, the Honourable Minister of Foreign Affairs, Shishir Khanal, responded to the questions raised by the following Honourable Members during the discussion on the bill:-\nHon. Lima Adhikari (Acharya)\nHon. Barsaman Pun\nHon. Padma Kumari Aryal\nHon. Basu Maya Tamang\nHon. Ganesh Bahadur Bishwakarma\nHon. Pushparaj Kandel\nHon. Yagyamani Neupane\nHon. Rima Bishwakarma\nHon. Ganga Lakshmi Awal\nHon. Rekha Kumari Yadav\nHon. Nishkal Rai\nHon. Prem Bahadur Bayak\nHon. Nirasha Chaudhary Dagaura\nHon. Pramila Kumari Gachhadar\nHon. Harka Raj Rai\nHon. Renuka Kaucha\nHon. Narendra Kumar Kerung\nHon. Tara Bishwakarma\nHon. Madhav Bahadur Thapa\nHon. Ambika Devi Sangraula\nHon. Madan Krishna Shrestha\nHon. Eshuda Kumari Baral\nHon. Tuka Bhadra Hamal\nHon. Mohan Lal Acharya\nHon. Amrita B.K.\nHon. Ganesh Karki\nHon. Saraswati Lama\nHon. Radhika Ramtel\nHon. Purna Prasad Limbu\nHon. Shajida Khatun Siddiki\nHon. Shahjan Khatun\nHon. Parashmani Gelal\nHon. Parbati B.K.\nThereafter, the Right Honourable Speaker put the proposal \"Consider the Passport (First Amendment) Bill, 2083\" to a decision, and it was approved by a majority.\nSubsequently, the Right Honourable Speaker informed that Honourable Members wishing to give notice of amendments to the \"Passport (First Amendment) Bill, 2083\" as per Rule 112 of the House of Representatives Regulations, 2083, could submit their notice to the Bill Section (House of Representatives), Federal Parliament Secretariat, Singh Durbar.\nAfter that, the Right Honourable Speaker informed the House that the programs listed as items 4 and 5 of today's agenda have been removed from the list.\nThereafter, the meeting was adjourned at 4:14 PM, with the next meeting of the House of Representatives scheduled to be held on Wednesday, Bhadra 3, 2083, at 1:00 PM.\nPanch Prasad Pandey\nSecretary-General\n",
